  "description": "Use of the existing flat roof as a roof terrace with 1.7m high trellis with ivy, 1.1m high railings and new access door",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The proposed terrace with associate boundary treatment, by reason of its scale, location and detailed design, would result in an uncharacteristic, overly cluttered and incongruous addition, that would disrupt the historic form of the site and surrounding area and fail to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the site and the wider Conservation Area and setting of the neighbouring Listed Buildings. As such the proposed development is contrary to policies D1 (London’s form, character, and capacity for growth), D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach), D4 (Delivering good design) and HC1 (Heritage, conservation and growth) of the London Plan (2021) and policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character) and LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020) and the Hackney Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (2025)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The proposed rear terrace with associated boundary treatment, by reason of its inappropriate positioning, scale and design would have a harmful impact to the living conditions of adjoining residential occupiers by reason of a loss of noise, privacy and overlooking. This is contrary to Policies LP2 (Development and Amenity), LP58 (Improving the Environment - Pollution) of the Hackney Local Plan LP33 (2020) and D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach), D6 (Housing quality and standards) and D14 (Noise) of the London Plan (2021) and the Hackney Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (2025).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
